From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:06:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: pure dial-screen key and Recents privacy model for
 Phone

Pure Java under sable/ for the next patch:

* SableDialpadKeys: the dial character a hardware key types. The Alt
  layer (Alt+W E R S D F Z X C = 1-9, the key map's Alt 0) types digits
  anywhere on the dial screen, from the event's character or, for the
  phone-pad letters, by key code; plain W E R S D F Z X C are 1-9 only
  while the dial pad has focus. Number row, numpad, *, # and + keep
  their characters; Shift+letter and Ctrl/Meta/Fn chords never type a
  digit. opensDialpad() says when a key on the main screen opens the
  dial pad with its digit.
* SableRecentsPrivacy: Recents hides who called while the device is
  locked or Sable private mode (read-only from Sable Hub) is on; no Hub
  means no private mode, an unexpected provider value means on.
---
 .../dialer/sable/SableDialpadKeys.java        | 140 ++++++++++++++++++
 .../dialer/sable/SableRecentsPrivacy.java     |  55 +++++++
 2 files changed, 195 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 java/com/android/dialer/sable/SableDialpadKeys.java
 create mode 100644 java/com/android/dialer/sable/SableRecentsPrivacy.java

